# Caddy reverse proxy for the "lite" showcase stack (single e2-micro VM), with automatic HTTPS
# (Let's Encrypt) for a real domain. Just one hostname, routed straight to the console.
#
# Unlike the book/logs stacks there is NO split-issuer trick here: auth is handled by hosted Auth0,
# whose issuer is a public URL that the browser and the hippocampus container reach identically.
# So Caddy needs no compose-network aliases, and there is no auth. or grafana. subdomain to route.
#
# Requires a public DNS A/AAAA record for the hostname pointing at the VM, with ports 80/443
# reachable (for the ACME challenge).
{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL:admin@example.com}
}

{$LITE_DOMAIN:hippocampus.example} {
	reverse_proxy hippocampus:8080
}
